            "review_title": "Review at Hao Yu Grilled Fish",
            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nUnique cuisine great for parties and sharing\nJun 2019 • Friends\nHad a craving for this grilled fish for quite some time ever since I tried it in China. So glad Hao Yu opened here in HCMC, and also an outlet in Phu My Hung in District 7. The restaurant's deco is pretty, a clever touch of the classic Chinese royal blue wall tiles shaped to look like fish scales and red wooden beams... pretty instagrammable.\n\nTheir Sichuan-flavoured fish was pretty on point, a good kind of spicy that keeps you wanting more with each bite. The tender fish definitely added to the addictive nature of this dish. If you prefer non-spicy versions, their tau xi flavour was pretty good too.\n\nOnce, I ordered this dish to-go for a party, and was rather pleased with their packaging. The sauce, peppers, grilled fish and sides were all packed separately and neatly, making it easy to assemble the dish later on. Pretty reasonable price of about 500,000vnd for a unique cuisine and rather large fish that stuffed four of us to the brim.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 2, 2019",
